From 0df6f0000a8a0d315034b6923671ef1b81d900e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chaton <definitelyfrenchname@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 01:46:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] cps2w: the CPS-2 WIDE SDRAM placement (slice D2)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Places the CPS-2 WIDE romset in the 64 MB SDRAM tier, per
docs/project/mister_map.md section 5 in the Vampire Saved repository. No
fetch changes: the obj promote that READS group C is slice D3, so this
commit is provable by the SDRAM image alone and is proven that way (an
image census of all four banks after download, byte for byte).

Everything with a behavioural surface is gated on `wide_en`, the runtime
profile bit slice D1 decodes out of MRA header byte 41. With it clear —
which is every stock MRA, by construction, because the generator fills the
header with 0xFF and the bit is active low — every expression below reduces
to the reference core's.

cores/cps2w/hdl/jtcps1_prom_we.v (NEW override of cores/cps1/hdl)
  * GFX group C -> banks 0 and 1. Vanilla's own 32 MB fills banks 2+3
    exactly, so the profile's group C (GFX region bytes 32-48 MB,
    gfx_addr[25]=1) has nowhere to go there. Obj bank 4 (gfx_addr[23]=0)
    goes to bank 1 above the 8 MB of QSound; obj bank 5 goes to bank 0.
  * QSound split on pcm_addr[23]: DSP sample banks 0x00-0x7F stay at bank 1
    offset 0, byte-identical to stock jtcps2; banks 0x80+ go to a 1 MB
    window in bank 0, masked to it. jtframe's 8-bit SDRAM slot caps at
    SDRAMW=23 (jtframe_romrq_bcache.v:74), so 8.9375 MB is only reachable
    as two slots in two banks.

cores/cps2w/hdl/jtcps1_sdram.v (NEW override of cores/cps1/hdl)
  * bank-0 re-pack to make room for a 6 MB PRG region: VRAM 0x600000,
    OBJ RAM 0x640000, work RAM 0x648000, Z80 0x658000, QSound high window
    0x6E0000, GFX group C obj bank 5 0x7E0000 (byte offsets).
  * the read side of both redirects, and the two new slot counts.
  * rom0_bank widened to 3 bits; bit 2 selects group C and is tied low by
    the game top until slice D3.
  The re-pack is UNCONDITIONAL because SLOTn_OFFSET are elaboration-time
  parameters. It is a relocation, not a behaviour change: the 68k sees the
  same data at the same addresses, VRAM/ORAM/WRAM are never downloaded, the
  Z80 region's download and read use the same constant, and bank 0 is the
  one bank with JTFRAME_BA0_AUTOPRECH=1, so its per-access latency is
  address-independent.

cores/cps2w/hdl/jtcps2_game.v
  wide_en routed to the SDRAM block, the full 24-bit qsnd_addr handed over
  for the split, rom0_bank presented as {1'b0, rom0_bank}.

modules/jtframe/hdl/sdram/jtframe_ram1_7slots.v (NEW)
  A mechanical member of the existing ram1_Nslots family — ram1_5slots with
  two more read-only slots and nothing else. Upstream stops at 5; bank 0
  now needs seven streams. Nothing that already existed was modified: the
  new module is pulled by cores/cps2w/cfg/game.yaml alone and NOT added to
  jtframe's shared jtframe_sdram64.yaml, so no other core's file list moves.

cores/cps1, cores/cps2 and cores/cps15 stay BYTE-UNTOUCHED.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01C93kTvSDUfHLL5sbjrArzn
